    {
      "data": {
        "body": "<h2>One governed front door</h2><p>Each object type has a strict body schema, a small set of typed patch operations, reference rules, creation policy, and publication policy. Agents read the live contract, validate candidates, edit under a lease, publish dark exports, and release a verified batch.</p><h2>Software is shared; tenants are isolated</h2><p>Core packages own rendering and publishing behavior. Each site owns its content, policies, credentials, stores, exports, and deployment. A core fix propagates through fleet CI without mixing tenant data.</p>"
